# Test: a BFD auth secret-hex that is not a binary string in hexadecimal is
# refused by `ze config validate`, and the refusal names the leaf.
#
# VALIDATES: RFC 5880 Sections 6.7.2, 6.7.3 and 6.7.4 -- the management
#            interface "SHOULD also allow for the configuration of any
#            arbitrary binary string in hexadecimal form." Ze takes that form
#            in the `secret-hex` leaf, and a value with an odd digit count has
#            no byte-for-byte decoding, so the config is refused rather than
#            run with a key the operator did not write.
# PREVENTS:  a malformed hex key truncated or padded into a different key,
#            which would leave the session down with no error naming why.

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bfd {
    enabled true;
    profile keyed {
        auth {
            type keyed-sha1;
            key-id 7;
            secret-hex "00ff7";
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=secret-hex
